  "prefLabel": "Ins 210.06 Explanation of the Rule",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 210.06 Explanation of the Rule. The department shall provide, if requested by any person at any time before 30 days after the final adoption of the rule, an explanation of the rule, including:\n\n(a) A concise statement of the principal reasons for and against the adoption of the rule in its final form; and\n\n(b) An explanation of why the department overruled the arguments and considerations against the rule, if any.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
